	TITLE	ASSEMBLY AND LOADING PROCEDURE				/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ THE NORMAL PROCEDURE FOR ASSEMBLING THE VISTA PROGRAM IS AS FOLLOWS:	/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ 	.R PAGE8							/01.32
/ 	*VISTA,LPT:VISTA<DEV:VISTA,VISTB,VISTC(IG)			/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ THE NORMAL PROCEDURE FOR ASSEMBLING THE VCM FILE IS:			/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ 	.R PAGE8							/01.32
/ 	*VCM0,LPT:<VISTA.SD,DEV:VCM52(IY)				/01.32
/ 									/01.33
/ ALTERNATIVELY, THE VCM FILES CAN BE ASSEMBLED WITH PAL8:		/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ 	.R PAL8								/01.32
/ 	*VCM0,LPT:<VISTA.EQ,DEV:VCM52.PA				/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ THE NORMAL PROCEDURE FOR LOADING THE BINARY FILES IS:			/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ 	.R ABSLDR							/01.32
/ 	*CL0.BN,CL1.BN							/01.32
/ 	*VISTA.BN/R$							/01.32
/ 	.SAVE SYS VISTA;1=0						/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ AND FOR THE VCM FILE:							/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ 	.R ABSLDR							/01.32
/ 	*CL0.BN								/01.32
/ 	*VCM0.BN/R$							/01.32
/ 	.SAVE SYS VCM0 6000-6577;7605					/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ IN THIS CASE, 'CL0.BN' AND 'CL1.BN' ARE TRIVIAL LITTLE BINARY FILES	/01.32
/ THAT FILL ALL OF FIELD 0 AND FIELD 1 RESPECTIVELY WITH ZEROES. THIS	/01.32
/ MAINTAINS THE DISC CONVENTION THAT ALL UNUSED MEMORY LOCATIONS ARE	/01.32
/ SET TO ZERO. 								/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ THE VISTA MANUAL CAN BE GENERATED WITH ACID AS FOLLOWS:		/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ 	.R ACID								/01.32
/ 	*LPT:<DEV:VDOCT(INZL)=5						/01.32
/ 									/01.32
/ 	.R ACID								/01.32
/ 	*LPT:<DEV:VDOCA,VDOCB,VDOCC(ZL)=7				/01.32
